Hmm, after reconsidering the above comments, now I am skeptical about introducing the per link online state. The link online state can be easily obtained from operstate and the required operstate rage of the link.

So, how about to introduce online state only on manager? Something like the following.
```
static int link_is_online(Link *link) {
        assert(link);

        if (!link->network || link->network->unmanaged || !link->network->required_for_online)
                return -ENODATA; /* arbitrary negative errno. */

        return operstate >= link->network->required_operstate_for_online.min &&
                operstate <= link->network->required_operstate_for_online.max;
}

int manager_save(Manager *m) {
        ...
        HASHMAP_FOREACH(link, m->link) {
                ...
                r = link_is_online(link);
                if (r > 0)
                        links_online++;
                else if (r == 0)
                        links_offline++;
}
```
Then, I think the logic seems quite simple.

